    "abstract": "Parts list for the cargo door latching mechanism, listing the retaining angle in its greased-bush and self-lubricating-bush standards as alternates against the bush modification.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the detail parts of the cargo door latching mechanism, including the latch shaft bearing installation and the warning sensor target plate.",
      "figure_note": "Item 20 and item 20A are alternates selected by the bush standard of the aircraft: item 20 is the deeper-spigot retaining angle used with the self-lubricating bush and item 20A is the earlier item used with the greased bush. The grease nipple that was a detail of item 20A does not exist on item 20 and there is no lubrication point on a door at the later standard; an order placed from the pre-modification item number will bring a rib the bush cannot be staked into. Bushes are supplied as a matched set of four and single-bush replacement is not permitted. The figure covers one door; both cargo doors use the same parts list."
    },
